== R104: lines 9864-10154; title 4878 B, sha1 654e32650985
   [title, l. 9864] ### R104 [refereed-only] N5 (SPEC S1-S5 from a GIVEN start pair, under the standing SPEC premise of RESULTS R57 (1E-N3: «that S1's procedure realises an optimal σ̄ is VJ00 §6 plus SPEC conformance», RESULTS R57 (b), read on every valid input of S1's procedure (Lead reading L45, RESULTS R102), used in two forms: S1's σ̄, and τ̄ on the dual game, are pointwise optima; and S4a's σ_new, S1's output on the dual of the one-player arena in which Even y keeps {σ(y)} ∪ Iσ(y) and Odd follows τ, is a pointwise optimum of that arena, before S4c), with RESULTS R24 (a) Lemma R and R24 (b)'s choice rule (TB proof steps 1, 3-5; fixes §2.3) with RESULTS R103's bridge B, whose proof uses no 𝒞^1O hypothesis (Lead reading L46 and its amendment), applied at every Even vertex that is not its own W′-cycle node, non-movers included (RESULTS R103's (R1) ruling), and with local optimality in a one-player game (RESULTS R36 (c) Lemma P1, applied on the dual game to Odd's one-player game against a fixed σ; VJ00's two-player Lemma 5.8 is not used)) realises the IDEAL model of L-RED R178 §1 on acyclic Ξ-graphs: an IDEAL genome G has N movers x with levels lev(x), M := Σ deg(x) options (x, k), each with a W-target of level lev(x) − 1 (none at level 0), a Ξ-target xt(x, k), a mover or the exit X, a distinct β-rank with a parity, a distinct gate index, and a start; under a state s the Ξ-value of option (x, k) is the set of β's on its chain (x, k), (xt, s(xt)), … up to the first Ξ-target X, compared by the β of largest rank in the symmetric difference: the option whose set contains that β is the better one if its parity is even and the worse one if odd; an IDEAL step moves every mover to the lexicographically least key (gate indices of the chain of W-targets under the new state, lowest level first) among its current option and the options with a strictly better Ξ-value, and the run stops when nothing is available or nothing changes, L(G) := its number of steps; the Ξ-graph has an edge x → xt(x, k) for every option with a mover as Ξ-target; for every G whose Ξ-graph is ACYCLIC, the game Γ(G) on n = N + 3M + 6 vertices (Even movers of priority 0; Odd gates of priority 1 with a W-face e and a Ξ-face β; β of priority 6 + 2·rank + parity with edges to the Ξ-target and to u, or to u alone; e of even priority above every β with one edge to the W-target or to the top even self-loop c_W; an unused even self-loop of priority 2; c_W's priority top is the least even number at least 2 above every other priority so far; a closed core u = K0 (Even, top + 2) → {K1, K3}, K1 (Even, 5) → {K0, K1}, K2 (Odd, 3) → {K1, K2}, K3 (Even, top + 3) → {K1, K2}; vertex indices: movers, gates in gate-index order, β-vertices, e-vertices in the order of their gates' gate indices, the unused loop, c_W, K0 to K3 (packet §3.1), on which the root-first key comparison depends) with start σ = the genome start at movers, β → its Ξ-target (u when the target is X), K0 → K3, K1 → K1, K3 → K2, τ = e at every gate and K2 → K2, has (Theorem REALIZE) an N5 run whose states 0, …, L(G) carry the IDEAL states at the movers, Odd's optimal counterstrategy on the β-face at every gate (strict local preference), τ unchanged (no Odd-improving edge), σ unchanged off the movers, the valuation of the (σ, τ)-play unchanged at every vertex, no fallback before state L(G) and a fallback at transition L(G) + 1, so, if L(G) ≥ 1, [0, L(G)] is one FL run (a maximal set of consecutive non-fallback transitions that keep τ, change σ and keep that valuation everywhere) of length exactly L(G) (no FL run if L(G) = 0); hence (Corollary REAL-IDEAL) if every FL run of N5 from every start pair on every n-vertex game has length at most p(n) for a nondecreasing polynomial p, then L(G) ≤ p(3(N + M) + 6) for every acyclic G, and a family of acyclic genomes with L super-polynomial in N + M is a family of real games with super-polynomially long FL runs from the stated start pairs (2026-11-02) — a REDUCTION / NECESSITY statement only (no count is bounded; Ξ-cyclic genomes are not covered; nothing about N5's default start S3; the converse is not claimed; DATA: random Ξ-cyclic genomes do mismatch; per-lemma checks with 0 violations on the 7 L-RED R178 champions (L 17 to 64), 2 L-RED R188 genomes, 60 random and 60 perturbed acyclic genomes; pins stab_d4_n126 (06f81991…, L_FL 32), stab_g24_n246 (55295dd8…, L_FL 64), x3_L8_n48 (158ca15d…), g4_L12_n62 (658f4e23…), each with a validated start and checked against Oink 8fbf0a7 --zlk / --tl with verify and two N5 engines; G-N5-TIME stays OPEN; not M3, not a step-4 pass, not a TARGET.md claim) (P-N5-REALIZE, docs/red/P-N5-REALIZE.md with its fixes entries 1-3, docs/red/P-N5-REALIZE-fixes.md; L-RED successors 44-45), CHECKER PASS (docs/checker/C115.md, checker 7c3c413f)
== R118: lines 13607-13878; title 6421 B, sha1 ddeb3b0db2ad
   (a) [l. 13677] (a) Definitions (§2 l. 52-66) [every genome]: IDEAL-CYC(G) («The game is Γ(G) with every Even vertex that is not a mover frozen at its start successor. Odd is unrestricted (gates and K2).»); a Howard step («every mover x goes to a successor of ⊴-largest Ω_t value, and keeps σ_t(x) if σ_t(x) is such a successor»; T_CYC := the number of steps to the first state where no mover has a strictly better successor); the labels («C if Λ_t(v) ≠ Λ_(t+1)(v) for some vertex v;», «else R if σ̄_t(v) ≠ σ̄_(t+1)(v) for some Odd vertex v;», «else p.»); n := N + 3M + 6, n_E the number of Even vertices.
   (b) [l. 13682] (b) Facts F1-F6 (§3 l. 68-83) with F4 REPLACED by F4′ (fixes l. 33-41): «if v ∉ Π(A) ∪ Π(B), then A ⊴ B ⇒ ext(v, A) ⊴ ext(v, B), and A ◁ B ⇒ ext(v, A) ◁ ext(v, B).» F4 as printed is false (REFEREE's instance, fixes l. 31-32: «A = (w, ∅, 3) ▷ B = (w, {v, y}, 3), but ext(v, A) ◁ ext(v, B).»); every §4 use and Corollary T3's use satisfy F4′ (movers have priority 0, below every cycle node; PATH's non-mover z_0 is in neither Π), fixes l. 37-42 and both referees.
   (c) [l. 13686] (c) Lemmas DOM, STRICT, PATH (§4 l. 86-101) [IDEAL-CYC, every genome]: DOM «For every mover x, step t and successor y of x: Ω_(t+1)(x) ⊵ ext(x, Ω_t(y)).»; STRICT «If σ_(t+1)(x) ≠ σ_t(x), then Ω_(t+1)(x) ▷ Ω_t(x).»; PATH: Ω_t(z_0) ⊵ val(π) along a simple path π of the fixed-σ̄ graph to a fixed cycle node, once t − a ≥ μ(π) (Bellman-Ford induction).
   (d) [l. 13689] (d) Theorem BR-SEG (§4 l. 102-111) [every genome]: «If Λ and σ̄ are constant on the states a, a+1, …, a+j+1 and the step a+j → a+j+1 changes σ, then j ≤ N − 1. Hence every maximal run of consecutive p-steps has at most N steps.»
   (e) [l. 13691] (e) Lemma CYC-COUNT (§4 l. 112-117): «C ≤ n·(2M + 2).» (each vertex's Λ moves only to a vertex of strictly larger reward among at most 2M + 3 possible cycle nodes).
   (i) [l. 13697] (i) Theorem BR-SEG-G (§5 l. 133-149; proof replaced by fixes l. 43-60) [any parity game, Howard from any σ_0, under H0]: «H0: every step t → t+1 switches some Even x with Λ_t(x) ≠ x and Λ_(t+1)(x) ≠ x.»; «(a) every maximal run of p-steps has at most n_E steps;», «(b) C ≤ n(n − 1);», «(c) T ≤ C + R + (C + R + 1)·n_E.» The packet's proof («§4's proofs, with «mover» read as «Even vertex»») uses DOM, which is false on general games (REFEREE §2.1 instance; REFEREE-2 G-1, r2dompex.out); the proof of record is STRICT-G and PATH-G (fixes l. 48-58), which use only F1, F3, F5 and F4′; «No DOM is used in §5 or §6.» (l. 60).
== R121: lines 14320-14743; title 5528 B, sha1 87298f60ff5f
   (a) [l. 14473] (a) Definitions (§2 l. 51-63): seq_t(v) «the e-vertices that lie in Π_t(v), in the order of the play from v under (σ_t, σ̄_t)», E_t(v) their set; lex order on sets of e-vertices; ascents («An ascent of a sequence (c_1, …, c_p) of distinct items is an index i with c_(i+1) more relevant than c_i.», l. 55); U_w, M_w, D_E,I(v); CS(M) («items 1..M, compared by number («rank»)», l. 58), forests and chains («A forest is a map next: items → items ∪ {⊥} without cycles. chain(x) := the sequence x, next(x), next²(x), … (as a set when compared).», l. 59), runs (l. 60-61), hubs and their values («A hub of a run is a choice h_t ∈ items ∪ {⊥} with chain_s(h_s) ≤ chain_t(h_t) for s < t (chain(⊥) := ∅). Its value at t is chain_t(h_t).», l. 62); the whole-run D_E(v) defined by fixes entry 1 AS-4 («the number D_E(v) of distinct (Λ_t(v), E_t(v))», l. 59).
   (b) [l. 14480] (b) Lemma E-MON (§3 l. 66-78) [IDEAL-CYC, every genome]: «If Λ_t(v) = Λ_(t+1)(v), then E_t(v) ≤ E_(t+1)(v).»; its proof contains the E-DOM step from R104's priorities («Every vertex more relevant than some e-vertex is an e-vertex, c_W, K0 or K3, by [DEF]», l. 70). REFEREE SIGN (l. 9), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 15).
   (c) [l. 14483] (c) Lemma CHAIN-DECOMP (§3 l. 80-88) [IDEAL-CYC]: «If seq_t(v) = (f, …), then the successor y_f of f is a mover, Λ_t(y_f) = Λ_t(v) and E_t(v) = {f} ∪ E_t(y_f).» «Hence seq_t(v) = (f, seq_t(y_f)).»; with the packet's «Reading» (l. 89-90: next_t is one forest on the e-vertices with cycle node w, every seq_t(v) a path of it), labelled Reading in the packet and checked by both referees (REFEREE l. 73-74; REFEREE-2 l. 55-56). The Reading is not a clause of the line («A RESULTS line carries signed statements only.», CHECKER C135 l. 32); it is a proof step of HUB-ASC-G («At each t ∈ I, next_t on the active items is one forest (CHAIN-DECOMP)», packet l. 156). The line states the lemma with the packet's hypothesis «seq_t(v) = (f, …)» alone (R5, then R-I) and its second sentence (R3). REFEREE SIGN (l. 10), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 16).
   (d) [l. 14490] (d) Lemma SKELETON (a)-(c) (§4 l. 98-107) [any forest of CS(M)]: the τ-path lies on chain(x) in order; the segment elements z satisfy z < τ^(i+1)(x) and τ(z) = τ^(i+1)(x), and τ^(i+2)(x) < τ^(i+1)(x); the step from a nonempty segment into τ^(i+1)(x) is an ascent. With «τ(x) is non-decreasing in rank» and the level count (§4 l. 94-96). REFEREE SIGN (l. 11), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 17).
   (e) [l. 14493] (e) Theorem HUB-ASC(B) (§4 l. 109-147) [any run of CS(M) with a hub]: «In any run of CS(M) with a hub whose value has at most B ascents at every time, the hub takes at most F_B(M) distinct values.» with F_0(M) := 1 + M(M + 1)/2 (B = 0: DESC-POLY), F_B(M) := (M² + M + 1)(1 + M·F_(B−1)(M)²), «For fixed B, F_B is a polynomial in M of degree 5·2^B − 3.»; the line gives CS(M)'s order and its ascents («items 1..M compared by number», «an ascent a step to a larger item», R-A) as §2 l. 55 and l. 58 define them, and its forests, chain(x), the hub with its condition and the hub's value («a forest a map next from the items to the items and ⊥ without cycles», «chain(x) := (x, next(x), next²(x), …) up to ⊥, compared as a set», «a hub (h_t an item or ⊥ at each time t, chain(⊥) := ∅, with chain_s(h_s) ≤ chain_t(h_t) for s < t) whose value chain_t(h_t)», R6) as §2 l. 59 and l. 62 define them. REFEREE SIGN (l. 12), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 18).
   (f) [l. 14501] (f) Corollary HUB-ASC-G (§5 l. 150-163) [every genome G, every vertex v and every interval I of states with Λ_t(v) = w]: «If seq_t(v) has at most B ascents for every t ∈ I, then D_E,I(v) ≤ F′_B(M_w).», F′_0 := 1 + M(M + 1)/2 (= F_0; by fixes entry 1 AS-1 «DESC-POLY on the whole interval», l. 54-56), F′_B(M) := (M² + 3M + 1)(1 + M·F′_(B−1)(M)²), «No hypothesis is made on any other vertex's plays.»; the whole-run corollary «D_E(v) ≤ (2M + 3)·F′_B(M)» from R118 (e). REFEREE SIGN (l. 13), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 19).
   (g) [l. 14505] (g) Lemma UP-JUMP (§6 l. 166-177) [under [E-LEV]]: an ascent a → b of seq_t(v) with a = e_(x,k), ℓ := lev(x), uses «a β-vertex whose Ξ-target is a mover of level > the level of the mover it was entered from, and ≥ ℓ». Corollary UP-B (§6 l. 179-185) [under [E-LEV]]: «every seq_t(v) has at most U(G) ascents, so D_E(v) ≤ (2M + 3)·F′_(U(G))(M) for every vertex v.». Corollary NOUP (§6 l. 187-188) [under [E-LEV], by W-1 in the packet's §1 and table too]: if U(G) = 0, every seq_t(v) is descending and «D_E(v) ≤ (2M + 3)(1 + M(M + 1)/2).». REFEREE SIGN (l. 14, «each under [E-LEV]»), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 20, «(each under [E-LEV])»).
   (h) [l. 14510] (h) Hypothesis [E-LEV] (§1 l. 46-48, as fixed by entry 1 W-1): «lev(x) < lev(x′) implies pr(e_(x,k)) < pr(e_(x′,k′))»; a hypothesis of UP-JUMP, UP-B and NOUP only, not in a landed R-id; §3-§5 do not use it (REFEREE l. 53-55; REFEREE-2 l. 40-41, its CTRL=elevrev control: §3-§5 counters stay 0; L-RED R220 §4).
== R123: lines 15076-15370; title 5512 B, sha1 5c12b6cf6768
   (a) [l. 15165] (a) Lemma CN2 (§2 l. 80-81) [every genome, every positional pair]: «For every genome G, every positional pair of IDEAL-CYC(G) and every vertex v, the cycle node of v's play has priority ≥ 2. So no gate (priority 1) and no mover (priority 0) is ever a cycle node, and no gate or mover is ever in a set Π.». REFEREE SIGN (l. 9), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 23).
   (b) [l. 15168] (b) Lemma B-ONLY (fixes entry 1 l. 11-12; L-RED R221 §3, re-derived) [every genome, every state of IDEAL-CYC]: «In IDEAL-CYC(G), for every genome G, every state t and every vertex v other than c_W and the e-vertices whose successor is c_W, Λ_t(v) is less relevant than every e-vertex (it is a β-vertex, K1, K2 or the unused loop).». REFEREE SIGN (l. 12), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 26).
   (c) [l. 15171] (c) Corollary NO-TIE (fixes entry 1 l. 26): «At every state and every gate g, Ω_t(e_g) ≠ Ω_t(β_g). So LOC-GATE applies at every gate and state.». REFEREE SIGN (l. 13), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 27).
   (d) [l. 15173] (d) Lemma LOC-GATE (§3 l. 89-90) [every genome, every state]: «Let G be any genome, t a state of a run of IDEAL-CYC(G), g a gate, a := σ̄_t(g), b := its other face, Ω := Ω_t. If Ω(a) ≠ Ω(b), then Ω(a) ◁ Ω(b).»; with NO-TIE the chosen face is the strictly ⊴-smaller one at every gate and state (the line's form). REFEREE SIGN (l. 10), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 24).
   (e) [l. 15176] (e) Lemma LOC-K2 (§3 l. 113): «At every state σ̄_t(K2) = K1 and Ω_t(K1) ◁ Ω_t(K2).». REFEREE SIGN (l. 11), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 25).
   (f) [l. 15177] (f) Theorem QUIET (§4 l. 119-122, 130, with fixes entry 1's (Q5) / (Q3) consequences) [every genome]: with class_t(v) := (Λ_t(v), E_t(v)), loud and quiet steps and quiet windows as defined (l. 119-120), «Every quiet window has at most L := (M + 1)(2M + 1)(N + 1) + N(n − 1) steps (n = N + 3M + 6).»; with NO-TIE, «(Q5): «flips at most twice … (to a tie, then to e)» becomes «at most once (β to e)»; G_C changes at most M times; at most M + 1 sub-windows; the stated L stays a valid (larger) bound.» (fixes l. 31-32). With the boundary step of fixes entry 3 (R-G repair: «Read (Q5)'s «by (Q4)'s argument and simplicity» as including this step. No statement changes.», fixes l. 127). REFEREE SIGN (l. 14; the step §3 l. 118-120), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 28; the step Add. 3 l. 398-399).
   (g) [l. 15183] (g) Corollary T-QUIET (§4 l. 131): «T ≤ Q + (Q + 1)·L ≤ (1 + Σ_v (D^tot_E(v) − 1))·(L + 1).», D^tot_E(v) «the number of distinct classes of v over the run» (l. 121). The line states the second bound. REFEREE SIGN (l. 15), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 29).
   (h) [l. 15185] (h) Corollary ASC-T (§5 l. 170-171) [premise RESULTS R121]: «If for every vertex v every seq_t(v) has at most B ascents, T ≤ (1 + n·((2M + 3)·F′_B(M) − 1))·(L + 1).». REFEREE SIGN, conditional on R121 (l. 16, §3 l. 136; §D l. 284: «provided it lands after R121»); REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 30, l. 142-146).
   (i) [l. 15188] (i) Corollary UP-T (§5 l. 165-166) [under HYPOTHESIS [E-LEV]; premise RESULTS R121]: «For every genome G, T ≤ (1 + n·((2M + 3)·F′_(U(G))(M) − 1))·(L + 1), with F′ as in P-N5-ASC §5. For genomes with U(G) ≤ B, B fixed, this is a polynomial in N + M.». REFEREE SIGN under HYPOTHESIS [E-LEV], conditional as ASC-T, plus UP-B (l. 17, §3 l. 137); REFEREE-2 SIGN, under HYPOTHESIS [E-LEV] (l. 31).
== R126: lines 15726-15902; title 7266 B, sha1 0deddcd9f217
   (a) [l. 15781] (a) Theorem GATE-CLASS (§2 l. 78-79) [every genome]: «For every genome G, every gate g and every step t of IDEAL-CYC(G): if σ̄_(t−1)(g) ≠ σ̄_t(g), then class_(t−1)(e_g) ≠ class_t(e_g) or class_(t−1)(β_g) ≠ class_t(β_g).» Both SIGN (REFEREE l. 10; REFEREE-2 l. 17).
   (b) [l. 15783] (b) Corollary GATE-FLIP (a) (§3 l. 102) [every genome]: «(a) flips(g) ≤ (D^tot(e_g) − 1) + (D^tot(β_g) − 1) for every gate g.» Both SIGN (l. 11; l. 18).
   (c) [l. 15785] (c) Corollary GATE-FLIP (b) (§3 l. 103-104) [under its ascent hypothesis; the U(G) form under HYPOTHESIS [E-LEV]]: «(b) If every seq_t(e_g) and every seq_t(β_g) has at most B ascents, then flips(g) ≤ 2·((2M + 3)·F′_B(M) − 1); under [E-LEV] (HYPOTHESIS, as in R121 / R123), B = U(G) may be taken.» Proof: (a) with R121's whole-run form for v = e_g, β_g, and R121's UP-B. REFEREE SIGN (l. 12), REFEREE-2 SIGN (l. 19).
   (d) [l. 15789] (d) Corollary QUIET-N (§4 l. 110-111) [every genome; sharpens RESULTS R123 Theorem QUIET / Corollary T-QUIET]: «In IDEAL-CYC(G), for every genome G: every quiet step is a p-step of R118; every maximal window of quiet steps has at most N steps; and T_CYC ≤ Q + (Q + 1)·N, where Q := the number of loud steps, Q ≤ Σ_v (D^tot(v) − 1).» Both SIGN (l. 13; l. 20). The «Against R123» bullet's «R123's ASC-T and UP-T hold with L + 1 replaced by N + 1.» (l. 119) is not in «To sign», not signed and not in L-1 or L-2 (LN-4; fixes l. 38-39).
   (e) [l. 15793] (e) Lemma (k+1)-Λ (§5 l. 123-125 as governed by fixes entry 1, l. 17) [every genome; k the Ξ-feedback number, packet (D5)]: «For every genome G with Ξ-feedback number k and every state t of IDEAL-CYC(G), the cycle nodes Λ_t(v), over all vertices v other than c_W, c_X and the e-vertices whose successor is c_W, take at most k + 1 values: K1, and, for each cycle of the functional graph Ξ_σ on the movers, x → xt(x, σ_t(x)), the most relevant vertex of the Γ-cycle through its movers, their chosen gates and β-faces; Ξ_σ has at most k cycles.» The frozen §5 named «the most relevant vertex of each cycle of the functional graph Ξ_σ on the movers», a mover (QN-1 = W-1); the proof is unchanged. REFEREE SIGN with QN-1 (l. 14), REFEREE-2 SIGN WITH W-1 (l. 21); both on the corrected wording (REFEREE §C LN-2 PASS; REFEREE-2 Add. 1 R-1 MET).
   (f) [l. 15800] (f) DEAD D1, D3 (§6 l. 137-147; the packet's D2 is not in L-2: fixes entry 2, C140 E-1 under L43): D1 «at k = 1 each gate flips at most 2·lamch(g) + 1 times» (k1fail_202, gate (4, 0): 2 flips, lamch 0); the packet's D2 «at k = 1 every gate flips at most c·(lamch(g) + 1) times», every constant c, rests on MWR4/8/16_2 (9 / 17 / 33 flips at lamch 0), which L-2 carries as DATA (the C = 0 clause, with L-RED 63's source, R-S); D3 «Every e-sequence has at most k + 1 ascents» (ST4_k1 3, ST8_k1 7 ascents at k = 1; WC4/8/16_2 4 / 8 / 16 at k = 2). REFEREE CONFIRMED on its own engine (l. 15, D3's k = 2 family cited), REFEREE-2 SIGN (dead) (l. 22); «D3's k = 2 WC family is re-run by neither referee. It is cited, and ST(m) kills D3 alone.» (REFEREE-2 Add. 2, l. 198). Re-signed on L-2 as D1, D3: REFEREE §D (l. 166-167, quoted in the SECOND FILL section) and REFEREE-2 Add. 3 (D1 and D3 «SIGN (dead)», l. 224 and 229; D1 re-run on its own GATE engine, l. 226-227).
